#* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:Robert Williams Buchanan|Robert [Williams] Buchanan]]|title=The Land of Lorne, Including the Cruise of the “Tern” to the Outer Hebrides.{{nb...|By Robert Buchanan. In Two Volumes.}}|volume=II|location=London|publisher=[[w:Chapman & Hall|Chapman and Hall]],{{nb...|193, Piccadilly.}}|year=1871|page=186|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/landlorneinclud00unkngoog/page/n200/mode/1up|passage=“Gathered in circle, / With clangour of armour, / Our youth struck the mighty / '''Donners''' of armlets: / Limbs dead and bloody / Glutted the death-birds. / Who shall avenge now / The mighty belt-wearer?”}}
