#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Seven Recruits Join Army on Wednesday|journal=[[w:The Atlanta Journal-Constitution|The Atlanta Constitution]]|volume=LII|issue=18|location=Atlanta, Ga.|date=3 July 1919|page=twenty|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/per_atlanta-constitution_1919-07-03_52_18/page/n19/mode/1up|passage=Seven recruits were accepted by the United States army at the Transportation building Wednesday. Of the seven new '''donners''' of the khaki, six were old service men.}}
